---
// One-line "what this tab does" explainer, rendered at the top of a dashboard panel.
//
// Shown ONLY while the seller's onboarding checklist is still incomplete (the parent decides) —
// so a first-time seller is told what every tab is for, and an established seller never carries
// the extra line. Same derived signal as the checklist, so nothing is stored or dismissed.
//
// **It is the sheet's own top band, not a paragraph floating above it** (owner, 2026-08-24: *"לא
// יושבות טוב על הקונטיינר... עם בורדר רדיוס עליון ושיתלבשו על גבי הקונטיינר הכללי"*). As a plain
// `<p>` inside the panel's padding it read as a stray line with the real content starting below it —
// and worse, it displaced `.dash-panel-head`, which by design IS the sheet's top edge and carries
// its border and its two top corners. So when this is first in a panel it takes that role instead:
// the geometry lives in `dashboard.css` under `.dash-tab-hint`, beside the `.dash-panel-head` rule
// it mirrors, because both are statements about the same edge and two copies of it is how the two
// would start disagreeing.
interface Props {
  text: string;
}
const { text } = Astro.props;
---

{/* `mb-3` is the SPACING FOR THE PLAIN CASE and has to stay: Overview's hint is not first in
    its panel and neither is any hint on a layout without the side rail, so most of the time
    this really is just a line of text that needs a gap under it. The band rule in
    `dashboard.css` sets `margin-block` and is unlayered, so it wins over a Tailwind utility
    whatever the specificity (`project_unlayered_css_beats_utility`). */}
{/* No colour utility on the element itself: it is `--color-muted` as a plain line and the
    surface colour inside the navy band, and a Tailwind `[color:…]` here would beat neither
    (unlayered CSS wins) nor be overridable per state. `dashboard.css` sets both. */}
<p class="dash-tab-hint flex items-start gap-[0.4rem] m-0 mb-3 text-[0.82rem] leading-[1.5]">
  <svg class="shrink-0 mt-[0.15rem]" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
    <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8"/>
  </svg>
  <span>{text}</span>
</p>
